        "original_id": "5fc76b28-774a-5571-9e98-864102a19e72",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Music Forms: Geetam\n- People: Purandara Dasa\n- Topics: Carnatic music, talas, sahityam, Haridasa, Krishna, Vishnu\n\nFacts:\n- Purandara Dasa lived from 1484 to 1564.\n- Purandara Dasa was a Haridasa, a devotee-servant of Lord Hari, who is Vishnu.\n- Purandara Dasa was a saint and a great devotee of Lord Krishna, an incarnation of Vishnu.\n- Geetam is the simplest music form in Carnatic music.\n- Purandara Dasa created Geetam to introduce talas together with sahityam, or lyrics.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
